[- Playground page. Interactive pane at the top; documentation below. -]
[page id='playground'
  [meta
    title='Playground'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='110'
    audience='evaluator,learner'
  ]

  [cx-playground]

  [section id='how' title='How This Works'
    [prose The playground runs entirely in the browser. Pick a starter example from the dropdown, edit it in the Source pane, and the three output tabs underneath show the canonical CX form, the JSON projection, and the XML projection of the parsed tree. No server, no signup.]
    [prose Sixteen starter examples ship in the corpus today — seven CX shapes (atom, attributes, sigils, typed table, anchor and merge, mixed content, multi-document) and nine CXL snippets (substitute, ?for, multi-branch ?if, ?let, filter pipeline, named template, CXPath axes and predicates, cx:merge, includes). Edit any of them in place; the Run button replays the example output today, and the v0.7.x WebAssembly build of libcx will route the same button through a live evaluator.]
  ]

  [section id='offline' title='Offline'
    [prose The browser playground is a static page. Clone the repo, render the doc tree with make docs, and serve _site/ from any HTTP server — the playground works without an internet connection. The example corpus, the TypeScript bundle, and the CSS all live under scripts/gen_docs/playground/.]
  ]

  [section id='highlight' title='Syntax Highlighting'
    [prose Every code block on this site is syntax-highlighted by a tiny in-house JS module at scripts/gen_docs/highlight/. It speaks the languages the docs actually use — cx, cxl, shell, python, go, rust, javascript, typescript, java, c-sharp, ruby, kotlin, swift, v, sql, ebnf, xml, html, json, yaml, toml, md. The highlighter is regex-based, around 150 lines, no external library. The Playground panes use the same module on every Run.]
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Where to Next'
    [list
      [item path='tour/data'     label='50 Ways to Love Your CX Data — more example shapes']
      [item path='tour/programs' label='50 Ways to Love Your CXL Code — more directives']
      [item path='install'       label='Install — run cx locally with the full evaluator']
      [item path='showcase'      label='Showcase — built-with-CX examples, including this doc-gen']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
